# =====================================================================
# kernel.clausal -- eu/aml/amlr_bo_chain SHARED FLOOR (the
# determination-slices DAG root; formerly schema.clausal).
# EMPTY BY MEASUREMENT, not by omission.
#
# WHY THERE IS NOTHING TO PUT HERE, by the recipe's decision procedure:
#
#  1. Does this domain MINT its own compound result constructor? NO. The
#     determination's answer channel is the 4th ARGUMENT of ubo_status/4 --
#     a bare atom, `eligible` or `ineligible` -- and of effective_ownership/4
#     -- an exact rational in basis points. There is no domain-owned
#     `X_verdict/N` / `X_result/N` term, and no element constructors
#     (`factor/2`, `obligation/2`, `cite/1`) for a consumer to pattern-match
#     by name. So the unconditional result-shape-constructor category is
#     EMPTY here. Rule 3 (input-constructor closure) has no instance either:
#     every argument the public predicates are queried with -- by
#     eval/score_harness.py, by tests/test_queries.clausal, and by the
#     bisect_flip/shrink_while closures in queries.clausal -- is a plain
#     list of [HOLDER, HELD, PCT_BPS] triples, a string, or an integer.
#
#  2. Do any VALUE ATOMS clear the strict ">= 2 SLICES" bar? NO -- this
#     domain has exactly ONE determination slice (ownership_interest.clausal,
#     the Art 52(1) ownership-interest test), so no name can be shared
#     between two slices. `eligible` / `ineligible` / `ubo_threshold_bps/1`
#     are spelled by the slice and by the TOP-LAYER consumer
#     queries.clausal; top-layer consumers do not count toward the kernel
#     bar, and they import those names from the owning slice instead.
#
# Kept as a file (rather than omitted) per the recipe's target layout, and
# because `auto/layout.py:is_sliced` reads `kernel.clausal`'s presence as
# THE marker that this tree is a determination-slice package -- without it
# `dag_order` falls back to the layer literal, which does not contain
# `ownership_interest` and would silently drop the slice from the package
# facade pkginit generates.
# =====================================================================

-module(kernel, [])
-double_quotes(chars)

-strict_atoms
